--TEST--
the file's own statements are a body like any other, so a cursor written between two of them offers the script frame's variables — `rule:ide/the-request-set-is-closed`, `rule:statements/storage-that-outlives-a-call`
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $name = "novis";
var $port = 8080;
<|>
echo $name;
--REQUEST--
completion prefix=$
--EXPECT--
$name   variable  string
$port   variable  int
